+## v42 root result and v43 repair
+
+Root reported that actual v42 check and build passed, but the native codegen suite passed only 50 of 53 tests. Its preserved log is `ROOT/candidate-unit-v42/codegen-native.log`. Three added fixtures expected one observation but observed zero: root native-import rejection, unavailable dependency traversal, and settled-negative dependency traversal. These results invalidate the v42 fixture gate, not establish a miss distribution or performance result.
+
+The semantic cause is the real store publication contract. In `ra-jit-store/src/lib.rs`, `Store::insert` appends to an open pack, whereas `Store::get` reads sealed packs. The existing native test `sealed_pack_is_named_by_its_bytes_and_read_back` explicitly asserts absence after insert and presence after publication. The v42 fixture helper inserted encoded parents/imported entries without publishing them. Consequently `usable` failed at the root get instead of reaching the import predicate or dependency traversal, explaining all three zero counters without changing their expectations.
+
+The v43 repair adds the actual native `Store::seal()` boundary to the fixture helper and asserts exact byte readback before exercising get/usable. Unlike flush with a size threshold, seal publishes however small the fixture pack. No native counter expectations are weakened, no production instrumentation or decisions change, and `mod.rs` stays byte-identical to frozen v42. Added store reads/publication are confined to `#[cfg(test)]` fixture setup, not disabled production code. Root must gate this new identity. Worker performed no native runs for the repair. The v43 archive retains exact failed v42 originals and the root failure log, plus repaired candidates, repair/full patches, hashes, and explicit readiness.
+
 ## Native fixture sources and root acceptance
 
 The added tests reside alongside the existing native `Entry` fixtures in `cached.rs`. They exercise the actual `Store::open_by_content`, insertion, native key computation, encoding/decoding, soundness, debug-type lookup, remapping, ban checks, get memoization, import predicate, and positive cyclic/transitive-negative usable traversal. There is no replacement decoder, mocked store, or copied SCC algorithm. Fixture counters are explicitly enabled on their own entries to avoid process-environment mutation. Source-only fixtures are not evidence that tests passed.
 
